  "lightingModel": "Sprites carry daylight only. Time of day is applied at runtime by multiplying the scene with a light map: the light map is filled with the ambient colour and each light source is added as a coloured radial gradient. Flames are drawn after the multiply so they stay bright. No per-time-of-day sprites.",
  "animation": {
    "fps": 8,
    "rules": [
      "Animated parts are separate layers or frames anchored to the same sprite anchor.",
      "Flames, smoke and banners animate; buildings stay static.",
      "Units use eight directions with the same projection and light as buildings.",
      "Loops must be seamless and last 4 to 12 frames."
    ]
  },
  "terrain": {
    "rule": "Ground is a flat 64 × 32 tile texture. Tiles of one set share a periodic colour field, so any two of them join without a seam.",
    "grass": "Lively mid-greens with darker patches; blades 2–9 px at 1×, drawn as small tufts; flowers sparse and pale. Avoid yellow-brown dry grass as the default.",
    "paths": "Wear goes from green through flattened dark green and olive to muted dark brown soil. Each stage is darker than the one before; no orange, red or bright tan (chroma at most 0.24).",
    "overgrowth": "An unused path recovers stage by stage back to grass (src/data/pathWear.js: recovery after 3 days, 5 points a day), so every stage must also read as a path growing over."
  },
  "units": {
    "rule": "Figures are 1.2 units tall (1.12 for women), face the camera and keep every part inside one tile.",
    "readability": "A profession must read at 1× from three cues at once: headgear, the tool or load in hand, and the main garment colour. Avoid recoloured clones.",
    "sexes": "Men wear a tunic over hose and may have a beard; women wear a long dress or kirtle, a coif or kerchief, often an apron. Tools and colours follow the profession, not the sex."
  },
  "props": {
    "rule": "Every production building tells its trade with two or three props in its yard: sacks, barrels, crates, hay, logs, an oven, ore, tools. Props stay inside the footprint and below the eaves, so the building keeps a clear silhouette."
  },
  "seasons": {
    "rule": "Seasons change the colour of grass, leaves and ground, never the silhouette of buildings. Spring is fresh light green with sparse blossom; summer is the lush base; autumn turns grass olive and leaves ochre, gold and russet (muted, never neon orange); winter dulls grass, bares broadleaf trees and adds snow in patches before full cover.",
    "transition": "A new season spreads over the first 10–25 % of its length, unevenly: each tile starts a little earlier or later by a stable hash and a slow large-scale noise, so the map never flips in one frame and shows no checkerboard. Paths, buildings and Fog of War memory keep their own rules."
  },
  "military": {
    "rule": "Military trades read through metal and order: racks of identical weapons, forges with glowing coals, stone and iron-banded doors. Soldiers differ by silhouette first (bow, spear-and-shield, sword-and-plate, horse), colour second (red for the crown, blue trim for knights)."
